// Brought to u by MidManStudio
//
// App-wide settings that aren't tied to any single note/todo — the
// counterpart to entry-note.mdix/entry-todo.mdix's per-entry `theme`
// field. Right now this only documents `theme` (the landing/list page's
// own default background, set from the Settings sheet — see
// settings.svelte.ts's appTheme). It deliberately does NOT also
// retrofit a schema for fontSize/debugPanelVisible/noteLinesEnabled:
// those already lived in settings.svelte.ts as plain localStorage
// values with no .mdix mirror before this file existed, and folding
// them in wasn't part of what this pass covered — doing that
// unasked would be guessing at a schema for fields nobody's confirmed
// need one yet. This file exists because `theme` specifically needed a
// real DixScript home (it reuses Themes.theme_preset()/theme_custom()
// from themes.mdix, same pointer shape as an entry's own theme), not as
// a claim that app settings as a whole are DixScript-backed now — they
// aren't; storage.ts/settings.svelte.ts are still the TEMPORARY
// localStorage layer, same as everything else pending
// src-tauri/src/data/entries.rs.

@CONFIG(
  version    -> "1.0.0"
  author     -> "Mid-D-Man"
  features   -> "data,imports,quickfuncs"
  debug_mode -> "off"
)

@IMPORTS(
  Themes from "themes.mdix"
)

@DATA(
  theme = Themes.theme_preset("none")
)
